  data:  # 3a07
    kind: work_item  # 3a07
    title: "message-queue linker topic_type=variable stores the variable identifier, not its resolved value"  # 3a07
    status: todo_hard  # 3a07
    priority: 2  # 3a07
    parent:  # 3a07
    tags:  # 3a07
    - dogfood  # 3a07
    isbefore: []  # 3a07
    duplicate_of: []  # 3a07
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 3a07
    pr_ref:  # 3a07
    description: "In the message-queue linker, when a publish topic is a variable, `topic_type=variable` is emitted and the stored topic value is the variable IDENTIFIER (`topic`/`TOPIC`/`EVENTS_TOPIC`) rather than its resolved string value; the same publisher emits both `literal` and `variable` for one logical topic depending on subscriber fan-out. A consumer joining publishers↔subscribers by topic value cannot match a variable-topic publish to its literal-topic subscriber. Fix: resolve the topic variable to its assigned value in message_queue.py topic extraction (or label it unresolved rather than storing the identifier as if it were the value). Surfaced via dogfooding; blinded severity 3/5."  # 3a07
    fields: {}  # 3a07
- op: discuss  # 4ab6
  at: '2026-10-01T00:55:20Z'  # 4ab6
  by: agent  # 4ab6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4ab6
  clock: 2  # 4ab6
  nonce: 4ab6  # 4ab6
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\n\nCode (unchanged in mechanism since filing; 12 commits touched the file since 06-07, none in topic extraction):\n- linkers/message_queue.py:291-311 _extract_topic_from_match returns (identifier, \"variable\") for a non-literal arg; nothing resolves it.\n- :106 MessageQueuePattern.topic is documented \"literal value or variable name\"; :478-480 copies it into Symbol meta topic/topic_type; :528-534 joins publishers to subscribers on the raw (queue_type, topic) string.\n- :558-561/:588 edge-level topic_type is \"variable\" if EITHER end is variable -- so the same publisher's edges carry literal or variable depending on which subscriber it joined (the item's fan-out claim, by mechanism).\n\nRepro (scratch fixture, link_message_queues called directly): pub.py `EVENTS_TOPIC = \"orders\"; producer.produce(EVENTS_TOPIC, msg)` plus `producer.produce(\"orders\", msg)`; sub.py `consumer.subscribe([\"orders\"])`.\n  SYM kafka:publish:EVENTS_TOPIC  topic=EVENTS_TOPIC topic_type=variable\n  SYM kafka:publish:orders        topic=orders       topic_type=literal\n  EDGE only literal publish(7) -> subscribe(2); the variable publish gets NO edge.\nSo the variable publisher is unmatched against its literal subscriber, as filed.\n\nUpdates for the item:\n- SAME MECHANISM IN TWO SIBLING LINKERS, not named in the item: linkers/ipc.py:305-323 (_extract_channel_from_match, channel_type \"variable\") and linkers/event_sourcing.py:132-138 (event_type \"variable\"). Rule 3: the fix (resolve a module-level string constant, or label the value unresolved) is a shared helper, not a message_queue.py edit.\n- Related open row, cite not fold: WI-vovob (meta.channel duplicates meta.topic on event_publishes edges).\n- Not re-measured: the dogfood frequency / severity 3/5."  # 4ab6
- op: update  # 5907
  at: '2026-10-01T01:33:47Z'  # 5907
  by: agent  # 5907
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5907
  clock: 3  # 5907
  nonce: '5907'  # 5907
  set:  # 5907
    title: "message-queue, ipc and event-sourcing linkers store a variable's identifier as the topic/channel/event value, not its resolved value"  # 5907
    description: "Three pub/sub-style linkers store a variable's IDENTIFIER where the joined value belongs. Surfaced via dogfooding on the message-queue linker; blinded severity 3/5.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, in message_queue.py: when a publish topic is a variable, `_extract_topic_from_match` (~L291-311) returns (identifier, \"variable\") -- the stored topic is `topic`/`TOPIC`/`EVENTS_TOPIC`, not the string assigned to it. `link_message_queues` joins publishers to subscribers on the raw (queue_type, topic) string (~L528-534), so a variable-topic publish never matches its literal-topic subscriber. The edge-level topic_type is \"variable\" if EITHER end is a variable (~L558-561, L588), so one publisher's edges carry `literal` or `variable` depending on which subscriber it joined.\n\nRepro (fixture, link_message_queues called directly): pub.py `EVENTS_TOPIC = \"orders\"; producer.produce(EVENTS_TOPIC, msg)` and `producer.produce(\"orders\", msg)`; sub.py `consumer.subscribe([\"orders\"])`. Result: symbol kafka:publish:EVENTS_TOPIC (topic=EVENTS_TOPIC, variable) gets NO edge; only the literal publish links to the subscriber.\n\nTHE SAME MECHANISM IN TWO SIBLING LINKERS:\n- linkers/ipc.py ~L305-323 `_extract_channel_from_match` -> channel_type \"variable\", channel = identifier.\n- linkers/event_sourcing.py ~L132-138 -> event_type \"variable\", event name = identifier.\n\nFix: one shared helper used by all three linkers that resolves a variable to its assigned string value (e.g. a module-level string constant), and labels the value unresolved -- rather than storing the identifier as if it were the value -- when it cannot. Not three local edits.\n\nRelated, cite do not fold: WI-vovob (meta.channel duplicates meta.topic on event_publishes edges).\nNot re-measured: dogfood frequency of the shape.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 5907
- op: discuss  # 19df
  at: '2026-10-02T00:47:36Z'  # 19df
  by: agent  # 19df
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 19df
  clock: 4  # 19df
  nonce: 19df  # 19df
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run; LOCAL branch jgstern-agent/fix/misod, commit f58e177598, not pushed, not merged; status unchanged).\n\nFix: new shared helper linkers/_name_args.py used by message_queue.py, ipc.py and event_sourcing.py. ConstantResolver resolves a call-site identifier to a SAME-FILE MODULE-SCOPE string constant (Python/JS/TS top-level assignment, Java static final String, Go const incl. const blocks) only when the file binds the name nowhere else; otherwise the site is labelled unresolved with value None and the identifier kept on a separate *_identifier key. pair_by_name joins on the VALUE when both sides know it, on the IDENTIFIER only when one side does not (kept so an imported constant still reaches its counterpart), never an identifier against a string. Site kinds: literal / constant / unresolved / variable (Django signal, Go channel). Also: MQ and event-sourcing edges now use each pattern's own symbol (a (path,line) index gave two same-line patterns one symbol).\n\nBehavior (live repro, filed fixture): before -- kafka:publish:EVENTS_TOPIC topic=EVENTS_TOPIC topic_type=variable, NO edge; after -- topic=orders topic_type=constant topic_identifier=EVENTS_TOPIC, edge to subscribe(['orders']) topic_match 0.9. IPC: const OPEN='open-file'; send(OPEN) -- before no edge, after ipc_channel_match 0.85. Event-sourcing: emit(CREATED) with CREATED='user:created' -- before joined on('created') (wrong edge, 0.65), after joins on('user:created') (0.85) only.\n\nTests: smart-test targeted, 560 files: 19888 passed, 3 skipped, 2 xfailed, changed files at 100% coverage. Three pre-existing tests that pinned the defect were reversed (MQ and IPC test_mixed_literal_and_variable_no_match asserted NO edge for constant-vs-literal; event-sourcing test_mixed_literal_variable_lower_confidence asserted the identifier-text join).\n\nA/B on 23 corpus repos under 200 MB (baseline = git archive of origin/dev; arms verified by imported module path + presence of _name_args): edge SETS identical in all 23 repos for all three linkers (MQ 17, IPC 75, ES 653 edges both arms; 0 added, 0 removed). 389 edges relabelled: 385 identifier-joined edges no longer assert the identifier as channel/topic/event_name (None + *_identifier), 5 ES edges move from identifier join 0.65 to value join 0.85. 21 sites resolve as constants (hand-checked 21/21 against their definitions). So the filed missed-edge shape and the identifier-text false join occur 0 times at edge level in this sample: a correct change with zero measured recall/precision effect on these repos; the measured effect is labelling. Not measured: repos outside the 23, survey-level outputs, slice.\n\nResiduals filed: WI-luhod-kibab-pizav-dubik-molaj-pihad-ditan-bujij (websocket.py + http.py, same mechanism), WI-fuduz-tokuj-najod-jagaf-guram-hival-zajav-sotas (imported / Class.ATTR / function-local constants stay unresolved; 1210 unresolved sites sized), WI-darom-rujil-kasal-fazod-damag-sipin-rohak-rugol (MQ JS .subscribe(x) FP on Svelte/RxJS). Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/misod.md"  # 19df
